    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-gated membership level 4 rule.\n\n**The rule now:** level starts at 1 and gains a point for each qualifying factor \u2014 a non-blank email, a unique name (`namesakeCount == 0`), and a three-or-more-member household (the GOLD factor documented on `Owner.householdMemberCount`). Level 4 is gated on tenure: it is only awarded when the owner has been registered for **more than 365 days**. Below that, the level is capped at 3. A newly created owner has zero tenure, so it can never exceed level 3 \u2014 even with an email, a unique name, and a three-member household (which would otherwise sum to 4), it lands at 3.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `MembershipLevelResolver.java` \u2014 added the household (GOLD) factor and the tenure gate. `deriveMembershipLevel` now takes `(email, namesakeCount, householdMemberCount, registrationDate)`; a `hasTenure` helper compares `registrationDate` to today via `ChronoUnit.DAYS`. Max level is 4 when tenured, 3 otherwise.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 updated the MapStruct `membershipLevel` expression to pass the household count and registration date.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 updated the audit-log call to the new signature, and moved `populateHouseholdMemberCount(owner)` ahead of it so the logged level reflects the real household size (removing the now-duplicate call).\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (new owner with an email \u2192 expects level 3) passes, and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3` for the freshly created owner.",
